{"title":"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Using_the_Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Using the Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Using_Heron&#39;s_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Using Heron's Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of the triangle with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/96195238f58bb95cdfffee45f4b29ae356cf1945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25, 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of the triangle with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d0f08e15f5cd4f0a7b123da3ebb667c56251e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25, 25,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the relationship between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418f02a2ff47a23b565b3935ad83dd7014b879c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } A = \\dfrac9{16}B \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } A = \\dfrac34B \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } A=B \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } A = \\dfrac43B \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }A = \\dfrac{16}9B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"640\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Using_the_Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Using_the_Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Using the Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Using the Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>25-25-30</b>\n</p><p>We can draw the altitude for the side with length 30. By HL Congruence, the two triangles formed are congruent. Thus the altitude splits the side with length 30 into two segments with length 15. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b2e5a4217d732c1e2542e1594940dac0c2190a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[15^2 + x^2 =25^2\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d747c318aae0a13969edabb764fbeb8f2c979322.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = 25^2 - 15^2\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96d946e9ed6cbba439bb205db2d285e76de80b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = (25 + 15)(25-15)\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1bba294ea8f5a3b77b090dc883eb2d26625710.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2= 40\\cdot 10\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6ebbd7ba07f85052c5fa3ffa25547aae332a1a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2= 400\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c6515fac376dc34f6af7fda7938e3c39c3bb87af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\sqrt{400}\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da648e1ee0029c7c1db961c89f1c6d031fe5d2dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x= 20\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThus we have two 15-20-25 right triangles.\n</p><p><b>25-25-40</b>\n</p><p>We can draw the altitude for the side with length 40. By HL Congruence, the two triangles formed are congruent. Thus the altitude splits the side with length 40 into two segments with length 20. From the 25-25-30 case, we know that the other side length is 15, so we have two 15-20-25 right triangles.\nLet the area of a 15-20-25 right triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d2522bf4fd5c76a00d3a0b8f6f262c7dd62f86f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 2x\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/a/78a5de5761fb75d82891f5c478373023b7accd5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b = 2x\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e441b3e971292f3ecad32f1ef93c26183bfb349.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } A = B}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Heron.27s_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Heron's_Formula)\">Solution 2 (Using Heron's Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Heron&#39;s Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using Heron's formula, we can calculate the area of the two triangles. The formula states that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca204d2647f51c17c25d3c7ece5b32a2803de98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\sqrt{s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)}\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"32\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the semiperimeter of a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>For the 25-25-30 triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9c4980866899235c62c482811afa640d921382c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = \\frac{25 + 25 + 30}{2} = 40\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"37\" />Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a632ffa6e6a41ac4ed5be20f1abfc679031bbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = \\sqrt{40 \\cdot 15 \\cdot 15 \\cdot 10} = 300\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>For the 25-25-40 triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad9ed4ad1a7e095f3215246cf5480c2415ed5c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = \\frac{25 + 25 + 40}{2} = 45\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"38\" />Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc47e0f658afcfc040af4c24e467d3123a468f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B = \\sqrt{45 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 5} = 300\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55aef7f707a0b354b9d0035bcab47547181e848c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = B \\hspace{0.15in} \\Longrightarrow \\hspace{0.15in} \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Simple)\">Solution 3 (Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b> Assume </b> the triangles are right. Then, the 25-25-30 has hypotenuse 30, whereas 25-25-40 has hypotenuse 40. Because the formula for a triangles' area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/1/7a1882918fcd74d05cbb55de8b7e904870fce028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(bh)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />, the hypotenuse does not matter. So, since the base and height are the same, the area will also be the same meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55aef7f707a0b354b9d0035bcab47547181e848c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A = B \\hspace{0.15in} \\Longrightarrow \\hspace{0.15in} \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYn6tNxrWBU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYn6tNxrWBU</a>\n</p><p><br />\n~SpreadtheMathLove\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UjACHET8l3E\">https://youtu.be/UjACHET8l3E</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8\">2011 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\